{
    "background_story": "Paloma was a skilled road engineer who spent her career designing and building highways across the country. Her specialty was bituminizing roads, a process that involved coating them with a layer of asphalt to protect them from the elements and extend their lifespan. Paloma took great pride in her work, knowing that her roads would connect communities and facilitate the transportation of goods and people. On one of her projects, she worked tirelessly to bituminize a rural road that had been damaged by floods. Her team worked through the night to complete the job, and when they finished, the local residents were overjoyed. Paloma's attention to detail and commitment to quality had transformed a treacherous road into a safe and reliable one, earning her the respect and gratitude of the community.",
